# Routing for Netlify. Cloudflare Pages reads the same syntax; Apache hosts use the
# rewrite block in .htaccess instead. Keep the three in step.
#
# "Pretty URLs" post-processing MUST BE DISABLED for this site
# (Site configuration > Build & deploy > Post processing > Asset optimization).
# It forwards /about to /about/, and a trailing slash would change every page's base
# directory from / to /about/ — harmless for root-absolute paths, but it also puts a
# slash in the address bar that nothing here wants. These rules state the mapping
# explicitly rather than depending on that setting.

# The old URLs keep working, so existing links and bookmarks survive.
# `!` is required: it forces the rule even though the .html file really exists.
/index.html                    /                              301!
/studios.html                  /studios                       301!
/production.html               /production                    301!
/about.html                    /about                         301!
/justin-souriau-levine.html    /justin-souriau-levine         301!

# Serve each page at its clean path. 200 rewrites, so the address bar keeps the clean URL.
/studios                       /studios.html                  200
/production                    /production.html               200
/about                         /about.html                    200
/justin-souriau-levine         /justin-souriau-levine.html    200
